				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\text{Pr}=1-\prod_{i=m}^{n-1}{e}^{{-r}_{i}}$$\end{document}Pr=1-∏i=mn-1e-riwhere m is the baseline age, n is the age at the end of follow-up and r is the birth year- and sex-specific population incidence at age i (in years). The expected number of cancer cases in the study sample is equal to the sum of the probabilities of all the participants.
